    "result_text": "The full test suite consists of `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are a base class and a helper) \u2014 all tests pass with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `contactPreference` field to the owner API: `EMAIL` when an email is on file, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nI followed the codebase's established pattern for derived owner fields (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`), which keeps the logic in one small, single-responsibility place and lets MapStruct auto-map it by name:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` getter that derives the value from the owner's own `email` field, mirroring the existing `getLocality()`/`getMembershipLevel()` derived getters (and reusing the same `email != null && !email.isEmpty()` check `getMembershipLevel` already uses).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived read-only fields, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and the existing `OwnerMapper` maps it automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\nNo new class or catch-all method was introduced \u2014 the rule lives on the domain object it's derived from.",
